PathwayData.put("data/grammar_vocabulary/units/L04U4.json",{"strand":"grammar_vocabulary","level":4,"cefr":"A2b","unit":4,"theme":"Adventures Outdoors","essential_question":"What can we learn from adventures in nature?","lessons":[{"id":"GV-L04-U4-LS1","title":"The Sun Was Setting: The Past Continuous","objectives":["Students will be able to form the past continuous with was/were + verb-ing.","Students will be able to describe actions in progress at a time in the past and set the scene in a story.","I can say \"At six o'clock, we were putting up the tent.\"","I can set the scene of a story with the past continuous."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من تكوين الماضي المستمر باستخدام was/were + الفعل مع ing.","سيتمكن الطلاب من وصف أفعال كانت مستمرة في وقت ما في الماضي ورسم مشهد القصة.","أستطيع أن أقول At six o'clock, we were putting up the tent.","أستطيع أن أرسم مشهد القصة بالماضي المستمر."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"camp","pos":"verb / noun","ipa":"/kæmp/","definition":"to stay outside in a tent; a place where people stay in tents","arabic":"يخيّم / مخيم","example":"We camped near the sand dunes.","image_id":"GV-L04-U4-LS1-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U4-LS1-W01"},{"word":"tent","pos":"noun","ipa":"/tɛnt/","definition":"a shelter made of cloth that you sleep in outside","arabic":"خيمة","example":"Dad put up the tent before dark.","image_id":"GV-L04-U4-LS1-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U4-LS1-W02"},{"word":"campfire","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈkæmpˌfaɪɚ/","definition":"a fire you make outside when you camp","arabic":"نار المخيم","example":"We made tea on the campfire.","image_id":"GV-L04-U4-LS1-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U4-LS1-W03"},{"word":"hike","pos":"verb / noun","ipa":"/haɪk/","definition":"to walk a long way in nature; a long walk","arabic":"يتنزّه سيرًا / نزهة طويلة","example":"We hiked to the top of the hill.","image_id":"GV-L04-U4-LS1-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U4-LS1-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"We use the past continuous for an action that was in progress at a time in the past: At six o'clock, Dad was putting up the tent. (He started before six and continued after.)\nForm: was / were + verb + -ing. I/he/she/it was walking; you/we/they were walking.\nIn stories, we use it to set the scene – to describe the background: The wind was blowing, and the stars were shining.\nI / he / she / it + was + verb-ing\nyou / we / they + were + verb-ing\nNegative: wasn't / weren't + verb-ing\nQuestion: Was/Were + subject + verb-ing?","examples":["At nine o'clock last night, I was reading a story.","The birds were singing when we woke up.","It was raining all afternoon.","My cousins were swimming in the lake.","What were you doing at five yesterday?","Grandpa wasn't sleeping; he was praying.","The stars were shining above the tent.","We were hiking along the trail at sunrise."],"common_errors":["✗ At six o'clock we was eating. → ✓ At six o'clock we were eating. (we → were.)","✗ She was cook dinner. → ✓ She was cooking dinner. (Add -ing.)","✗ I eating when you called. → ✓ I was eating when you called. (Don't forget was/were.)","✗ What you were doing? → ✓ What were you doing? (were before the subject in questions.)"],"arabic":"نستخدم الماضي المستمر لفعل كان مستمرًا في لحظة معينة في الماضي: At six o'clock, Dad was putting up the tent.\nالتركيب: was/were + الفعل مع ing، was مع المفرد وwere مع الجمع وyou.\nنستخدمه في القصص لرسم الخلفية: The wind was blowing."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “The Sun Was Setting: The Past Continuous”. Let’s learn past continuous (was/were + verb-ing) for actions in progress in the past together.","on_screen":"GV-L04-U4-LS1 | The Sun Was Setting: The Past Continuous","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Listen to the start of “A Night in the Desert”: Last winter, my family went camping near Al-Ula. At six o'clock, the sun was setting behind the rocks, and the sky was turning orange. Look at the green words.","on_screen":"Last winter, my family went camping near Al-Ula. At six o'clock, the sun was setting behind the rocks, and the sky was turning orange.","visual":"Image GV-L04-U4-LS1-IMG01 animates gently; target words glow Leaf Green as they are spoken."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"We use the past continuous for an action that was in progress at a time in the past: At six o'clock, Dad was putting up the tent. (He started before six and continued after.) Form: was / were + verb + -ing. I/he/she/it was walking; you/we/they were walking.","on_screen":"I / he / she / it + was + verb-ing • you / we / they + were + verb-ing • Negative: wasn't / weren't + verb-ing","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. At nine o'clock last night, I was reading a story. The birds were singing when we woke up. It was raining all afternoon.","on_screen":"At nine o'clock last night, I was reading a story. / The birds were singing when we woke up. / It was raining all afternoon.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “At six o'clock we was eating.” That’s not right. We say: “At six o'clock we were eating.” we → were.","on_screen":"✗ At six o'clock we was eating.   ✓ At six o'clock we were eating.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"At six, Dad was putting up the tent.\" Did he start before six? … Think! … Yes – it was in progress at six. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"At six o'clock, we were putting up the tent.\"","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say \"At six o'clock, we were putting up the tent.\"","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: past continuous (was/were + verb-ing) for actions in progress in the past.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نستخدم الماضي المستمر لفعل كان مستمرًا في لحظة معينة في الماضي: At six o'clock, Dad was putting up the tent.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: At six o'clock we was eating. — الصحيح: At six o'clock we were eating.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول At six o'clock, we were putting up the tent."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"A Night in the Desert","body":"Last winter, my family went camping near Al-Ula.\nAt six o'clock, the sun was setting behind the rocks, and the sky was turning orange.\nDad was putting up the tent while Mom was making tea on the campfire. My brother and I were collecting wood.\nSuddenly, we heard a strange noise. Something was moving behind a bush!\nI was holding my flashlight, so I pointed it at the bush. It was a little desert fox! It was looking for food.\nLater, while we were lying in our sleeping bags, we were still talking about our adventure.","word_count":96,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U4-LS1-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L04-U4-LS1-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"At 7 p.m., I ___ my homework.","options":["was do","was doing","were doing","did doing"],"answer":"was doing","explanation":"I / he / she / it → was + verb-ing.","explanation_ar":"was مع المفرد."},{"q":"The children ___ in the garden at noon.","options":["were playing","were play","was playing","played playing"],"answer":"were playing","explanation":"you / we / they → were + verb-ing.","explanation_ar":"were مع الجمع."},{"q":"It ___ when we left the house.","options":["was rain","was raining","were raining","rained raining"],"answer":"was raining","explanation":"Add -ing to the main verb.","explanation_ar":"أضف ing."},{"q":"We ___ sleeping. We were talking.","options":["wasn't","didn't","aren't","weren't"],"answer":"weren't","explanation":"wasn't / weren't + verb-ing.","explanation_ar":"النفي."},{"q":"___ you watching the match at eight?","options":["Are","Was","Were","Did"],"answer":"Were","explanation":"Was/Were + subject + verb-ing?","explanation_ar":"السؤال."},{"q":"My dad ___ the car when I saw him.","options":["was wash","washing","was washing","were washing"],"answer":"was washing","explanation":"I / he / she / it → was + verb-ing.","explanation_ar":"was مع المفرد."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U4-LS1-B1","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Write the past continuous. Word bank: were fishing, wasn't sleeping, was blowing","items":[{"q":"At midnight, the wind ______ (blow) hard.","options":[],"answer":"was blowing","explanation":"I / he / she / it → was + verb-ing.","explanation_ar":"was مع المفرد."},{"q":"My brothers ______ (fish) at sunrise.","options":[],"answer":"were fishing","explanation":"you / we / they → were + verb-ing.","explanation_ar":"were مع الجمع."},{"q":"I ______ (not / sleep) when you called.","options":[],"answer":"wasn't sleeping","explanation":"wasn't / weren't + verb-ing.","explanation_ar":"النفي."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U4-LS1-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Make questions.","items":[{"q":"You were reading at nine.  (question)","options":[],"answer":"Were you reading at nine?","explanation":"Was/Were + subject + verb-ing?","explanation_ar":"السؤال."},{"q":"Sara was painting. (What)","options":[],"answer":"What was Sara doing?","explanation":"Was/Were + subject + verb-ing?","explanation_ar":"السؤال."},{"q":"They were camping in Abha. (Where)","options":[],"answer":"Where were they camping?","explanation":"Was/Were + subject + verb-ing?","explanation_ar":"السؤال."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U4-LS1-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: What were you doing?","items":[{"q":"At 6:00 this morning, I was ___.","options":[],"answer":"At 6:00 this morning, I was praying Fajr.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past continuous (was/were + verb-ing) for actions in progress in the past correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"At 8:00 last night, my family was ___.","options":[],"answer":"At 8:00 last night, my family was eating dinner.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past continuous (was/were + verb-ing) for actions in progress in the past correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Yesterday afternoon, my friends were ___.","options":[],"answer":"Yesterday afternoon, my friends were playing football.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past continuous (was/were + verb-ing) for actions in progress in the past correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Last Friday at noon, I was ___.","options":[],"answer":"Last Friday at noon, I was visiting my grandparents.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past continuous (was/were + verb-ing) for actions in progress in the past correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"At 9:00 yesterday, my teacher was ___.","options":[],"answer":"At 9:00 yesterday, my teacher was teaching us grammar.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past continuous (was/were + verb-ing) for actions in progress in the past correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U4-LS1-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Set the scene.","items":[{"q":"Look at a camping picture. Write 4 sentences to set the scene.","options":[],"answer":"The sun was setting. A boy was sitting by the fire. His dad was cooking. A dog was sleeping near the tent.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past continuous (was/were + verb-ing) for actions in progress in the past correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 sentences about what was NOT happening.","options":[],"answer":"It wasn't raining. Nobody was talking.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past continuous (was/were + verb-ing) for actions in progress in the past correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Ask a partner \"What were you doing at … yesterday?\" Write his answer.","options":[],"answer":"At five yesterday, he was riding his bike.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past continuous (was/were + verb-ing) for actions in progress in the past correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Spin & Speak","mechanic":"spin_wheel","rules":["Work in teams of four. Player 1 spins the wheel.","Make a correct sentence about the unit theme using the cue word and past continuous (was/were + verb-ing) for actions in progress in the past.","The team checks the sentence with the grammar box. Correct = 1 point; an extra detail = 1 bonus point.","Pass the spinner clockwise. Play for 6 minutes; the team with most points wins."],"data":[{"label":"was walking"},{"label":"were sleeping"},{"label":"was raining"},{"label":"were talking"},{"label":"was cooking"},{"label":"was shining"},{"label":"were hiking"},{"label":"was reading"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"At 10 p.m., my sister ___ a book.","options":["were reading","read reading","was read","was reading"],"answer":"was reading","explanation":"I / he / she / it → was + verb-ing.","explanation_ar":"was مع المفرد."},{"q":"The boys ___ football in the park.","options":["was playing","were playing","playing was","were play"],"answer":"were playing","explanation":"you / we / they → were + verb-ing.","explanation_ar":"were مع الجمع."},{"q":"","options":["The sun was shining when we arrived.","The sun was shine when we arrived.","The sun were shining when we arrived.","The sun shining when we arrived."],"answer":"The sun was shining when we arrived.","explanation":"Add -ing to the main verb.","explanation_ar":"أضف ing."},{"q":"I ___ listening. Can you repeat it?","options":["not","weren't","didn't","wasn't"],"answer":"wasn't","explanation":"wasn't / weren't + verb-ing.","explanation_ar":"النفي."},{"q":"What ___ Grandpa doing in the garden?","options":["were","did","was","is was"],"answer":"was","explanation":"Was/Were + subject + verb-ing?","explanation_ar":"السؤال."},{"q":"","options":["We were walk along the trail.","We was walking along the trail.","We were walking along the trail.","We walking along the trail."],"answer":"We were walking along the trail.","explanation":"you / we / they → were + verb-ing.","explanation_ar":"were مع الجمع."},{"q":"","options":["Were they sleeping in a tent?","They were sleeping in a tent?","Was they sleeping in a tent?","Did they sleeping in a tent?"],"answer":"Were they sleeping in a tent?","explanation":"Was/Were + subject + verb-ing?","explanation_ar":"السؤال."},{"q":"The wind ___ all night.","options":["were blowing","was blowing","blowing","was blow"],"answer":"was blowing","explanation":"I / he / she / it → was + verb-ing.","explanation_ar":"was مع المفرد."},{"q":"","options":["My parents weren't watch TV at nine.","My parents wasn't watching TV at nine.","My parents weren't watching TV at nine.","My parents didn't watching TV at nine."],"answer":"My parents weren't watching TV at nine.","explanation":"wasn't / weren't + verb-ing.","explanation_ar":"النفي."},{"q":"At noon yesterday, I ___ in the pool.","options":["were swimming","was swimming","swimming","was swiming"],"answer":"was swimming","explanation":"Add -ing to the main verb.","explanation_ar":"أضف ing."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L04-U4-LS1-IMG01","prompt":"A desert campsite at sunset near the rocks of Al-Ula: a father putting up a tent, a mother making tea on a campfire, two boys collecting wood, and a small desert fox peeking from behind a bush. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A desert campsite at sunset near the rocks of Al-Ula: a father putting up a tent, a mother making tea on a campfire, two boys collecting wood, and a small desert fox peeking from behind a bush"},{"id":"GV-L04-U4-LS1-IMG02","prompt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about past continuous (was/were + verb-ing) for actions in progress in the past, with Zaki the Falcon pointing at a blank board on the right; leave large empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about past continuous (was/were + verb-ing) for actions in progress in the past, with Zaki the Falcon pointing at a blank board on the right"},{"id":"GV-L04-U4-LS1-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows camp (to stay outside in a tent; a place where people stay in tents); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing camp: to stay outside in a tent; a place where people stay in tents"},{"id":"GV-L04-U4-LS1-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows tent (a shelter made of cloth that you sleep in outside); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing tent: a shelter made of cloth that you sleep in outside"},{"id":"GV-L04-U4-LS1-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows campfire (a fire you make outside when you camp); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing campfire: a fire you make outside when you camp"},{"id":"GV-L04-U4-LS1-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows hike (to walk a long way in nature; a long walk); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing hike: to walk a long way in nature; a long walk"},{"id":"GV-L04-U4-LS1-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Spin & Speak”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Spin & Speak"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U4-LS1-W01","script":"camp. camp. We camped near the sand dunes.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U4-LS1-W02","script":"tent. tent. Dad put up the tent before dark.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U4-LS1-W03","script":"campfire. campfire. We made tea on the campfire.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U4-LS1-W04","script":"hike. hike. We hiked to the top of the hill.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U4-LS1-T1","script":"Last winter, my family went camping near Al-Ula. At six o'clock, the sun was setting behind the rocks, and the sky was turning orange. Dad was putting up the tent while Mom was making tea on the campfire. My brother and I were collecting wood. Suddenly, we heard a strange noise. Something was moving behind a bush! I was holding my flashlight, so I pointed it at the bush. It was a little desert fox! It was looking for food. Later, while we were lying in our sleeping bags, we were still talking about our adventure.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U4-LS1-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “The Sun Was Setting: The Past Continuous”. Let’s learn past continuous (was/were + verb-ing) for actions in progress in the past together. Listen to the start of “A Night in the Desert”: Last winter, my family went camping near Al-Ula. At six o'clock, the sun was setting behind the rocks, and the sky was turning orange. Look at the green words. We use the past continuous for an action that was in progress at a time in the past: At six o'clock, Dad was putting up the tent. (He started before six and continued after.) Form: was / were + verb + -ing. I/he/she/it was walking; you/we/they were walking. Here are some examples. At nine o'clock last night, I was reading a story. The birds were singing when we woke up. It was raining all afternoon. Be careful! Some learners say: “At six o'clock we was eating.” That’s not right. We say: “At six o'clock we were eating.” we → were. Quick check: \"At six, Dad was putting up the tent.\" Did he start before six? … Think! … Yes – it was in progress at six. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"At six o'clock, we were putting up the tent.\"","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.9"}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U4-LS2","title":"While We Were Hiking, We Saw a Snake: Past Continuous and Past Simple","objectives":["Students will be able to use the past continuous for a longer background action and the past simple for a short action that interrupts it.","Students will be able to join actions with when and while.","I can say \"I was walking when it started to rain.\"","I can say \"While we were hiking, we saw a snake.\""],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام الماضي المستمر للفعل الطويل والماضي البسيط للفعل القصير الذي يقطعه.","سيتمكن الطلاب من ربط الأفعال باستخدام when وwhile.","أستطيع أن أقول I was walking when it started to rain.","أستطيع أن أقول While we were hiking, we saw a snake."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"trail","pos":"noun","ipa":"/treɪl/","definition":"a path through the countryside or mountains","arabic":"درب / ممر","example":"Follow the trail to the waterfall.","image_id":"GV-L04-U4-LS2-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U4-LS2-W01"},{"word":"compass","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈkʌmpəs/","definition":"a tool that shows north, south, east and west","arabic":"بوصلة","example":"The compass helped us find the way.","image_id":"GV-L04-U4-LS2-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U4-LS2-W02"},{"word":"flashlight","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈflæʃˌlaɪt/","definition":"a small light you hold in your hand (American English)","arabic":"مصباح يدوي","example":"Turn on your flashlight in the cave.","image_id":"GV-L04-U4-LS2-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U4-LS2-W03"},{"word":"sleeping bag","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈslipɪŋ bæɡ/","definition":"a warm bag you sleep in when you camp","arabic":"كيس نوم","example":"My sleeping bag kept me warm all night.","image_id":"GV-L04-U4-LS2-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U4-LS2-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"When a short action happens in the middle of a longer action, use the past continuous for the longer action and the past simple for the short one: I was walking (long) when it started (short) to rain.\nwhen + past simple (the short action): We were eating when the lights went out. while + past continuous (the long action): While we were hiking, we saw a snake.\nTwo long actions happening at the same time: While Mom was cooking, Dad was reading.","examples":["We were camping when the storm started.","While I was climbing the rock, I slipped.","The phone rang while Dad was driving.","Lina was taking photos when a bird landed on her camera.","While we were eating, a cat came into the tent.","I saw a shooting star while I was looking at the sky.","While Mom was cooking, my brothers were setting the table.","What were you doing when I called?"],"common_errors":["✗ I walked when it was starting to rain. → ✓ I was walking when it started to rain. (Long action → past continuous; short action → past simple.)","✗ While I walked, I was seeing a fox. → ✓ While I was walking, I saw a fox. (while + past continuous; the short action → past simple.)","✗ When I was arriving, they were eating. → ✓ When I arrived, they were eating. (when + short action (past simple).)"],"arabic":"الفعل الطويل في الماضي المستمر، والفعل القصير الذي يقطعه في الماضي البسيط: I was walking when it started to rain.\nwhen غالبًا مع الفعل القصير (الماضي البسيط)، وwhile مع الفعل الطويل (الماضي المستمر).\nفعلان طويلان في الوقت نفسه: While Mom was cooking, Dad was reading."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “While We Were Hiking, We Saw a Snake: Past Continuous and Past Simple”. Let’s learn past continuous vs past simple with when and while together.","on_screen":"GV-L04-U4-LS2 | While We Were Hiking, We Saw a Snake: Past Continuous and Past Simple","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Remember these patterns: I was sleeping when the phone rang. • While she was swimming, she saw a turtle. I wasn't looking when he took the photo. What were you doing when the storm started?","on_screen":"I was sleeping when the phone rang. • While she was swimming, she saw a turtle. | I wasn't looking when he took the photo. | What were you doing when the storm started?","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"When a short action happens in the middle of a longer action, use the past continuous for the longer action and the past simple for the short one: I was walking (long) when it started (short) to rain. when + past simple (the short action): We were eating when the lights went out. while + past continuous (the long action): While we were hiking, we saw a snake.","on_screen":"past continuous vs past simple with when and while","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. We were camping when the storm started. While I was climbing the rock, I slipped. The phone rang while Dad was driving.","on_screen":"We were camping when the storm started. / While I was climbing the rock, I slipped. / The phone rang while Dad was driving.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “I walked when it was starting to rain.” That’s not right. We say: “I was walking when it started to rain.” Long action → past continuous; short action → past simple.","on_screen":"✗ I walked when it was starting to rain.   ✓ I was walking when it started to rain.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"I was walking when it started to rain.\" Which action is longer? … Think! … walking. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"I was walking when it started to rain.\"","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say \"I was walking when it started to rain.\"","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: past continuous vs past simple with when and while.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","الفعل الطويل في الماضي المستمر، والفعل القصير الذي يقطعه في الماضي البسيط: I was walking when it started to rain.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: I walked when it was starting to rain. — الصحيح: I was walking when it started to rain.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول I was walking when it started to rain."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L04-U4-LS2-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"I ___ TV when the power went off.","options":["watched","watch","were watching","was watching"],"answer":"was watching","explanation":"Long background action → past continuous.","explanation_ar":"الفعل الطويل ← الماضي المستمر."},{"q":"We were hiking when we ___ a snake.","options":["see","were seeing","saw","was seeing"],"answer":"saw","explanation":"Short action that interrupts → past simple.","explanation_ar":"الفعل القصير ← الماضي البسيط."},{"q":"___ I was sleeping, someone knocked on the door.","options":["During","Then","While","When"],"answer":"While","explanation":"while + past continuous.","explanation_ar":"while + الماضي المستمر."},{"q":"It was raining ___ we left the house.","options":["during","when","than","while"],"answer":"when","explanation":"when + past simple (short action).","explanation_ar":"when + الماضي البسيط."},{"q":"While Mom ___, Dad was cleaning.","options":["was cooking","cooked","cooks","were cooking"],"answer":"was cooking","explanation":"Two long actions at the same time → past continuous + past continuous.","explanation_ar":"فعلان طويلان معًا."},{"q":"He ___ when he was playing football.","options":["was falling","fell","falls","were falling"],"answer":"fell","explanation":"Short action that interrupts → past simple.","explanation_ar":"الفعل القصير ← الماضي البسيط."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U4-LS2-B1","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Write the past continuous or the past simple. Word bank: was sleeping, were swimming, found","items":[{"q":"While we ______ (swim), it started to rain.","options":[],"answer":"were swimming","explanation":"while + past continuous.","explanation_ar":"while + الماضي المستمر."},{"q":"I was walking home when I ______ (find) a wallet.","options":[],"answer":"found","explanation":"Short action that interrupts → past simple.","explanation_ar":"الفعل القصير ← الماضي البسيط."},{"q":"The baby ______ (sleep) when the doorbell rang.","options":[],"answer":"was sleeping","explanation":"Long background action → past continuous.","explanation_ar":"الفعل الطويل ← الماضي المستمر."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U4-LS2-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Join the sentences with when or while.","items":[{"q":"I was reading.  +  The lights went out.","options":[],"answer":"I was reading when the lights went out.","explanation":"when + past simple (short action).","explanation_ar":"when + الماضي البسيط."},{"q":"We were driving to Abha.  +  We saw monkeys.","options":[],"answer":"While we were driving to Abha, we saw monkeys.","explanation":"while + past continuous.","explanation_ar":"while + الماضي المستمر."},{"q":"Sara was painting.  +  Lina was writing.","options":[],"answer":"While Sara was painting, Lina was writing.","explanation":"Two long actions at the same time → past continuous + past continuous.","explanation_ar":"فعلان طويلان معًا."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U4-LS2-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Complete the stories.","items":[{"q":"I was walking to school when ___.","options":[],"answer":"I was walking to school when I saw a cat on a wall.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past continuous vs past simple with when and while correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"While we were having lunch, ___.","options":[],"answer":"While we were having lunch, my uncle arrived.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past continuous vs past simple with when and while correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"My brother was playing video games when ___.","options":[],"answer":"My brother was playing video games when Mom called him.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past continuous vs past simple with when and while correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"While I was sleeping, ___.","options":[],"answer":"While I was sleeping, it started to snow.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past continuous vs past simple with when and while correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"We were watching the match when ___.","options":[],"answer":"We were watching the match when our team scored.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past continuous vs past simple with when and while correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U4-LS2-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Tell a surprise story.","items":[{"q":"Write 4 sentences about a surprise that happened to you. Use when and while.","options":[],"answer":"I was doing my homework when I heard a noise. I went to the kitchen. While I was looking, a cat jumped out! It was our neighbor's cat.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past continuous vs past simple with when and while correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 sentences about two things happening at the same time.","options":[],"answer":"While I was studying, my sister was drawing. While Dad was driving, we were singing.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past continuous vs past simple with when and while correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Ask a partner \"What were you doing when…?\" Write his answer.","options":[],"answer":"He was sleeping when the alarm rang.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past continuous vs past simple with when and while correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Tic-Tac-Grammar","mechanic":"tic_tac_toe","rules":["Two teams: X and O. Team X chooses a square.","Using the cue, the team says a correct sentence with past continuous vs past simple with when and while (the form in brackets: +, – or ?).","If the class and teacher agree it is correct, the team marks the square.","Three squares in a row wins. Play a second round with the grid turned around."],"data":[{"cue":"I / walk / it / start to rain"},{"cue":"we / hike / we / see a snake"},{"cue":"Dad / cook / the fire / go out"},{"cue":"the boys / sleep / a noise / wake them"},{"cue":"she / read / the lights / go off"},{"cue":"they / swim / the whistle / blow"},{"cue":"the sun / set / we / reach the camp"},{"cue":"I / climb / I / slip"},{"cue":"it / snow / we / build a snowman"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"I ___ a shower when the phone rang.","options":["was taking","take","were taking","took"],"answer":"was taking","explanation":"Long background action → past continuous.","explanation_ar":"الفعل الطويل ← الماضي المستمر."},{"q":"We were walking in the park when it ___ to rain.","options":["were starting","started","starts","was starting"],"answer":"started","explanation":"Short action that interrupts → past simple.","explanation_ar":"الفعل القصير ← الماضي البسيط."},{"q":"___ they were hiking, they found an old coin.","options":["When","Before while","While","During"],"answer":"While","explanation":"while + past continuous.","explanation_ar":"while + الماضي المستمر."},{"q":"The lights went out ___ we were eating dinner.","options":["while","when","than","during"],"answer":"while","explanation":"while + past continuous.","explanation_ar":"while + الماضي المستمر."},{"q":"","options":["While I was cooking, my brother cleaning.","While I cooked, my brother was clean.","While I was cook, my brother was cleaning.","While I was cooking, my brother was cleaning."],"answer":"While I was cooking, my brother was cleaning.","explanation":"Two long actions at the same time → past continuous + past continuous.","explanation_ar":"فعلان طويلان معًا."},{"q":"","options":["She broke her arm when she skiing.","She was breaking her arm when she skied.","She broke her arm when she was skiing.","She was broke her arm when she was skiing."],"answer":"She broke her arm when she was skiing.","explanation":"Short action that interrupts → past simple.","explanation_ar":"الفعل القصير ← الماضي البسيط."},{"q":"","options":["What you were doing when the storm started?","What were you doing when the storm started?","What were you do when the storm started?","What did you doing when the storm started?"],"answer":"What were you doing when the storm started?","explanation":"Long background action → past continuous.","explanation_ar":"الفعل الطويل ← الماضي المستمر."},{"q":"While we ___ for the bus, a friend called us.","options":["was waiting","waited","were waiting","wait"],"answer":"were waiting","explanation":"while + past continuous.","explanation_ar":"while + الماضي المستمر."},{"q":"","options":["Dad driving when he saw the camels.","Dad drove when he was seeing the camels.","Dad was driving when he was see the camels.","Dad was driving when he saw the camels."],"answer":"Dad was driving when he saw the camels.","explanation":"when + past simple (short action).","explanation_ar":"when + الماضي البسيط."},{"q":"The bird ___ when I was taking its photo.","options":["flies away","were flying away","was flying away","flew away"],"answer":"flew away","explanation":"Short action that interrupts → past simple.","explanation_ar":"الفعل القصير ← الماضي البسيط."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L04-U4-LS2-IMG01","prompt":"A timeline drawing: a long wavy line labeled \"We were hiking\" and a short lightning bolt labeled \"we saw a snake\", with Yusuf and Adam on a rocky trail. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A timeline drawing: a long wavy line labeled \"We were hiking\" and a short lightning bolt labeled \"we saw a snake\", with Yusuf and Adam on a rocky trail"},{"id":"GV-L04-U4-LS2-IMG02","prompt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of past continuous vs past simple with when and while: a green tick panel and a soft red cross panel with simple objects from the theme “Adventures Outdoors”; empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of past continuous vs past simple with when and while: a green tick panel and a soft red cross panel with simple objects from the theme “Adventures Outdoors”"},{"id":"GV-L04-U4-LS2-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows trail (a path through the countryside or mountains); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing trail: a path through the countryside or mountains"},{"id":"GV-L04-U4-LS2-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows compass (a tool that shows north, south, east and west); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing compass: a tool that shows north, south, east and west"},{"id":"GV-L04-U4-LS2-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows flashlight (a small light you hold in your hand (American English)); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing flashlight: a small light you hold in your hand (American English)"},{"id":"GV-L04-U4-LS2-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows sleeping bag (a warm bag you sleep in when you camp); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing sleeping bag: a warm bag you sleep in when you camp"},{"id":"GV-L04-U4-LS2-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Tic-Tac-Grammar”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Tic-Tac-Grammar"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U4-LS2-W01","script":"trail. trail. Follow the trail to the waterfall.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U4-LS2-W02","script":"compass. compass. The compass helped us find the way.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U4-LS2-W03","script":"flashlight. flashlight. Turn on your flashlight in the cave.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U4-LS2-W04","script":"sleeping bag. sleeping bag. My sleeping bag kept me warm all night.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U4-LS2-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “While We Were Hiking, We Saw a Snake: Past Continuous and Past Simple”. Let’s learn past continuous vs past simple with when and while together. Remember these patterns: I was sleeping when the phone rang. • While she was swimming, she saw a turtle. I wasn't looking when he took the photo. What were you doing when the storm started? When a short action happens in the middle of a longer action, use the past continuous for the longer action and the past simple for the short one: I was walking (long) when it started (short) to rain. when + past simple (the short action): We were eating when the lights went out. while + past continuous (the long action): While we were hiking, we saw a snake. Here are some examples. We were camping when the storm started. While I was climbing the rock, I slipped. The phone rang while Dad was driving. Be careful! Some learners say: “I walked when it was starting to rain.” That’s not right. We say: “I was walking when it started to rain.” Long action → past continuous; short action → past simple. Quick check: \"I was walking when it started to rain.\" Which action is longer? … Think! … walking. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"I was walking when it started to rain.\"","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.9"}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U4-LS3","title":"Hike, Wander, Slip: Outdoor Words and Movement Verbs","objectives":["Students will be able to use outdoor and camping words.","Students will be able to choose precise movement verbs to describe how people move.","I can talk about camping and hiking.","I can choose between walk, hike, wander, crawl and slip."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام كلمات الرحلات الخلوية والتخييم.","سيتمكن الطلاب من اختيار أفعال الحركة الدقيقة لوصف طريقة الحركة.","أستطيع أن أتحدث عن التخييم والمشي في الطبيعة.","أستطيع أن أختار بين walk وhike وwander وcrawl وslip."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"backpack","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈbækˌpæk/","definition":"a bag you carry on your back","arabic":"حقيبة ظهر","example":"Put the water bottles in your backpack.","image_id":"GV-L04-U4-LS3-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U4-LS3-W01"},{"word":"cliff","pos":"noun","ipa":"/klɪf/","definition":"a high, steep rock face","arabic":"جرف / منحدر صخري","example":"Don't stand near the edge of the cliff.","image_id":"GV-L04-U4-LS3-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U4-LS3-W02"},{"word":"wildlife","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈwaɪldˌlaɪf/","definition":"animals and plants that live in nature","arabic":"الحياة البرية","example":"Farasan Islands have amazing wildlife.","image_id":"GV-L04-U4-LS3-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U4-LS3-W03"},{"word":"slip","pos":"verb","ipa":"/slɪp/","definition":"to slide by accident and almost fall","arabic":"ينزلق","example":"Be careful – you might slip on the wet rocks.","image_id":"GV-L04-U4-LS3-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U4-LS3-W04"},{"word":"wander","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˈwɑndɚ/","definition":"to walk slowly with no special plan","arabic":"يتجوّل","example":"We wandered around the old village.","image_id":"GV-L04-U4-LS3-W05","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U4-LS3-W05"}],"explanation":{"text":"Outdoor words: camp, tent, campfire, trail, compass, flashlight (American English), sleeping bag, backpack, cliff, wildlife.\nMovement verbs have shades of meaning. walk (normal) • hike (walk a long way in nature) • wander (walk slowly with no plan) • march (walk in step like soldiers). climb (go up using hands and feet) • crawl (move on hands and knees) • slide (move smoothly on a surface) • slip (slide by accident).\nChoosing a precise verb makes writing more interesting: He slipped on the wet rock (better than \"He moved\").\nCollocations/phrases: put up a tent • light a campfire • follow a trail • read a compass • turn on a flashlight • pack a backpack | walk → hike → march • wander (slowly, no plan) • climb (up) • crawl (hands and knees) • slide (smooth) • slip (by accident) | watch wildlife • reach the top • get lost • find the way","examples":["We put up the tent before sunset.","The scouts followed the trail to the valley.","I crawled into the small cave with my flashlight.","Grandpa likes to wander around the old market.","Be careful – you might slip on the ice.","The children slid down the sand dune.","We hiked for three hours to reach the top.","The compass showed us the way north."],"common_errors":["✗ We made a tent. → ✓ We put up a tent. (put up a tent.)","✗ My brother slipped down the slide on purpose. → ✓ My brother slid down the slide. (slip = by accident; slide = on purpose.)","✗ Bring a torch for the night. (American English) → ✓ Bring a flashlight for the night. (In American English, flashlight.)","✗ The baby is walking on his hands and knees. → ✓ The baby is crawling. (Hands and knees → crawl.)"],"arabic":"كلمات التخييم: tent (خيمة) وcampfire (نار المخيم) وtrail (درب) وcompass (بوصلة) وflashlight (مصباح يدوي).\nأفعال الحركة: hike (مشي طويل في الطبيعة) وwander (تجوّل بلا خطة) وcrawl (يزحف) وslip (ينزلق بالخطأ) وslide (ينزلق عمدًا).\nنقول put up a tent (ننصب خيمة) وليس make a tent."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Hike, Wander, Slip: Outdoor Words and Movement Verbs”. Let’s learn camping and outdoor vocabulary; verbs of movement with shades of meaning (walk, hike, wander, march; climb, crawl, slide, slip) together.","on_screen":"GV-L04-U4-LS3 | Hike, Wander, Slip: Outdoor Words and Movement Verbs","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Meet some new words. backpack: a bag you carry on your back. cliff: a high, steep rock face. wildlife: animals and plants that live in nature.","on_screen":"backpack | cliff | wildlife","visual":"Each word card flips over to show its picture (vocabulary image briefs) and Arabic meaning."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Outdoor words: camp, tent, campfire, trail, compass, flashlight (American English), sleeping bag, backpack, cliff, wildlife. Movement verbs have shades of meaning. walk (normal) • hike (walk a long way in nature) • wander (walk slowly with no plan) • march (walk in step like soldiers). climb (go up using hands and feet) • crawl (move on hands and knees) • slide (move smoothly on a surface) • slip (slide by accident).","on_screen":"camping and outdoor vocabulary; verbs of movement with shades of meaning (walk, hike, wander, march; climb, crawl, slide, slip)","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. We put up the tent before sunset. The scouts followed the trail to the valley. I crawled into the small cave with my flashlight.","on_screen":"We put up the tent before sunset. / The scouts followed the trail to the valley. / I crawled into the small cave with my flashlight.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “We made a tent.” That’s not right. We say: “We put up a tent.” put up a tent.","on_screen":"✗ We made a tent.   ✓ We put up a tent.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: Do you slip on purpose or by accident? … Think! … By accident. Great job! Now you can say: I can talk about camping and hiking.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can talk about camping and hiking.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: camping and outdoor vocabulary; verbs of movement with shades of meaning (walk, hike, wander, march; climb, crawl, slide, slip).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","كلمات التخييم: tent (خيمة) وcampfire (نار المخيم) وtrail (درب) وcompass (بوصلة) وflashlight (مصباح يدوي).","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: We made a tent. — الصحيح: We put up a tent.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أتحدث عن التخييم والمشي في الطبيعة."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L04-U4-LS3-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct word.","items":[{"q":"We ___ a tent near the lake.","options":["put up","did","built on","made"],"answer":"put up","explanation":"Use the right outdoor collocation.","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة الصحيحة."},{"q":"The baby can't walk yet. He ___ on the floor.","options":["marches","slips","crawls","hikes"],"answer":"crawls","explanation":"Choose the movement verb with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"فعل الحركة المناسب."},{"q":"The rocks were wet, and Ali ___.","options":["hiked","wandered","marched","slipped"],"answer":"slipped","explanation":"Choose the movement verb with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"فعل الحركة المناسب."},{"q":"A ___ shows north, south, east and west.","options":["flashlight","tent","trail","compass"],"answer":"compass","explanation":"Choose the camping word that fits.","explanation_ar":"كلمة التخييم المناسبة."},{"q":"We ___ ten kilometers in the mountains.","options":["hiked","crawled","slipped","slid"],"answer":"hiked","explanation":"Choose the movement verb with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"فعل الحركة المناسب."},{"q":"In American English, a small hand light is a ___.","options":["torch","flashlight","candle","lamp post"],"answer":"flashlight","explanation":"American English: flashlight.","explanation_ar":"الإنجليزية الأمريكية: flashlight."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U4-LS3-B1","type":"match","instructions":"Guided practice: Match the verb to the meaning.","items":[{"q":"wander","options":["move smoothly on a surface","walk in step like soldiers","walk slowly with no plan","go up using hands and feet","walk a long way in nature","move on hands and knees"],"answer":"walk slowly with no plan","explanation":"wander → walk slowly with no plan. Choose the movement verb with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"فعل الحركة المناسب."},{"q":"climb (a cliff)","options":["move smoothly on a surface","walk in step like soldiers","walk slowly with no plan","go up using hands and feet","walk a long way in nature","move on hands and knees"],"answer":"go up using hands and feet","explanation":"climb (a cliff) → go up using hands and feet. Choose the movement verb with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"فعل الحركة المناسب."},{"q":"slide","options":["move smoothly on a surface","walk in step like soldiers","walk slowly with no plan","go up using hands and feet","walk a long way in nature","move on hands and knees"],"answer":"move smoothly on a surface","explanation":"slide → move smoothly on a surface. Choose the movement verb with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"فعل الحركة المناسب."},{"q":"march","options":["move smoothly on a surface","walk in step like soldiers","walk slowly with no plan","go up using hands and feet","walk a long way in nature","move on hands and knees"],"answer":"walk in step like soldiers","explanation":"march → walk in step like soldiers. Choose the movement verb with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"فعل الحركة المناسب."},{"q":"hike","options":["move smoothly on a surface","walk in step like soldiers","walk slowly with no plan","go up using hands and feet","walk a long way in nature","move on hands and knees"],"answer":"walk a long way in nature","explanation":"hike → walk a long way in nature. Choose the movement verb with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"فعل الحركة المناسب."},{"q":"crawl","options":["move smoothly on a surface","walk in step like soldiers","walk slowly with no plan","go up using hands and feet","walk a long way in nature","move on hands and knees"],"answer":"move on hands and knees","explanation":"crawl → move on hands and knees. Choose the movement verb with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"فعل الحركة المناسب."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U4-LS3-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Write about outdoor adventures.","items":[{"q":"When we go camping, we take ___.","options":[],"answer":"When we go camping, we take a tent and sleeping bags.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses camping and outdoor vocabulary; verbs of movement with shades of meaning (walk, hike, wander, march; climb, crawl, slide, slip) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"I like to wander around ___.","options":[],"answer":"I like to wander around the old souq.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses camping and outdoor vocabulary; verbs of movement with shades of meaning (walk, hike, wander, march; climb, crawl, slide, slip) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"I once slipped on ___.","options":[],"answer":"I once slipped on a wet floor.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses camping and outdoor vocabulary; verbs of movement with shades of meaning (walk, hike, wander, march; climb, crawl, slide, slip) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"A place where I want to hike is ___.","options":[],"answer":"A place where I want to hike is Jabal Sawda.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses camping and outdoor vocabulary; verbs of movement with shades of meaning (walk, hike, wander, march; climb, crawl, slide, slip) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Some wildlife I saw on a trip was ___.","options":[],"answer":"Some wildlife I saw on a trip was a herd of oryx.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses camping and outdoor vocabulary; verbs of movement with shades of meaning (walk, hike, wander, march; climb, crawl, slide, slip) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U4-LS3-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Plan a camping trip.","items":[{"q":"Write a packing list of 6 things for a camping trip.","options":[],"answer":"tent, sleeping bags, flashlight, compass, water, backpack","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses camping and outdoor vocabulary; verbs of movement with shades of meaning (walk, hike, wander, march; climb, crawl, slide, slip) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 3 sentences about the trip with precise movement verbs.","options":[],"answer":"We hiked to the top. My brother slid down the dune. We wandered around the campsite.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses camping and outdoor vocabulary; verbs of movement with shades of meaning (walk, hike, wander, march; climb, crawl, slide, slip) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one safety tip with slip or cliff.","options":[],"answer":"Don't go near the cliff – you might slip.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses camping and outdoor vocabulary; verbs of movement with shades of meaning (walk, hike, wander, march; climb, crawl, slide, slip) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Memory Match","mechanic":"matching","rules":["Place all cards face down in a grid.","Turn over two cards. If the word matches its definition, keep the pair and say a sentence with the word.","If not, turn them back over; the next player plays.","The player with the most pairs wins."],"data":[{"word":"camp","match":"to stay outside in a tent; a place where people stay in tents","arabic":"يخيّم / مخيم"},{"word":"tent","match":"a shelter made of cloth that you sleep in outside","arabic":"خيمة"},{"word":"campfire","match":"a fire you make outside when you camp","arabic":"نار المخيم"},{"word":"hike","match":"to walk a long way in nature; a long walk","arabic":"يتنزّه سيرًا / نزهة طويلة"},{"word":"trail","match":"a path through the countryside or mountains","arabic":"درب / ممر"},{"word":"compass","match":"a tool that shows north, south, east and west","arabic":"بوصلة"},{"word":"flashlight","match":"a small light you hold in your hand (American English)","arabic":"مصباح يدوي"},{"word":"sleeping bag","match":"a warm bag you sleep in when you camp","arabic":"كيس نوم"},{"word":"backpack","match":"a bag you carry on your back","arabic":"حقيبة ظهر"},{"word":"cliff","match":"a high, steep rock face","arabic":"جرف / منحدر صخري"},{"word":"wildlife","match":"animals and plants that live in nature","arabic":"الحياة البرية"},{"word":"slip","match":"to slide by accident and almost fall","arabic":"ينزلق"},{"word":"wander","match":"to walk slowly with no special plan","arabic":"يتجوّل"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"We ___ the trail to the waterfall.","options":["did","made","slipped","followed"],"answer":"followed","explanation":"Use the right outdoor collocation.","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة الصحيحة."},{"q":"The soldiers ___ in the parade.","options":["marched","slipped","crawled","wandered"],"answer":"marched","explanation":"Choose the movement verb with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"فعل الحركة المناسب."},{"q":"The kids ___ down the snowy hill on a sled.","options":["slipped","crawled","slid","hiked"],"answer":"slid","explanation":"Choose the movement verb with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"فعل الحركة المناسب."},{"q":"Turn on your ___. It's dark in the cave.","options":["compass","backpack","trail","flashlight"],"answer":"flashlight","explanation":"Choose the camping word that fits.","explanation_ar":"كلمة التخييم المناسبة."},{"q":"A warm bag for sleeping outside is a ___.","options":["sleeping bag","compass","backpack","tent bag"],"answer":"sleeping bag","explanation":"Choose the camping word that fits.","explanation_ar":"كلمة التخييم المناسبة."},{"q":"Don't stand near the edge of the ___.","options":["campfire","compass","trail map","cliff"],"answer":"cliff","explanation":"Choose the camping word that fits.","explanation_ar":"كلمة التخييم المناسبة."},{"q":"We ___ a campfire to keep warm.","options":["put up","made up","lit","did"],"answer":"lit","explanation":"Use the right outdoor collocation.","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة الصحيحة."},{"q":"Which verb means \"walk slowly with no plan\"?","options":["wander","crawl","march","hike"],"answer":"wander","explanation":"Choose the movement verb with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"فعل الحركة المناسب."},{"q":"Oryx and falcons are part of Saudi ___.","options":["trails","wildlife","backpacks","campfires"],"answer":"wildlife","explanation":"Choose the camping word that fits.","explanation_ar":"كلمة التخييم المناسبة."},{"q":"The cat ___ up the tree to get the bird.","options":["slipped","climbed","wandered","marched"],"answer":"climbed","explanation":"Choose the movement verb with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"فعل الحركة المناسب."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L04-U4-LS3-IMG01","prompt":"A mountain trail scene with labeled actions: a boy hiking with a backpack, a girl wandering near flowers, a child crawling into a small cave with a flashlight, someone slipping on wet rocks, and a compass on a map. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A mountain trail scene with labeled actions: a boy hiking with a backpack, a girl wandering near flowers, a child crawling into a small cave with a flashlight, someone slipping on wet rocks, and a compass on a map"},{"id":"GV-L04-U4-LS3-IMG02","prompt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 5 small picture icons of the lesson words; empty labels. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 5 small picture icons of the lesson words"},{"id":"GV-L04-U4-LS3-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows backpack (a bag you carry on your back); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing backpack: a bag you carry on your back"},{"id":"GV-L04-U4-LS3-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows cliff (a high, steep rock face); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing cliff: a high, steep rock face"},{"id":"GV-L04-U4-LS3-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows wildlife (animals and plants that live in nature); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing wildlife: animals and plants that live in nature"},{"id":"GV-L04-U4-LS3-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows slip (to slide by accident and almost fall); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing slip: to slide by accident and almost fall"},{"id":"GV-L04-U4-LS3-W05","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows wander (to walk slowly with no special plan); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing wander: to walk slowly with no special plan"},{"id":"GV-L04-U4-LS3-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Memory Match”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Memory Match"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U4-LS3-W01","script":"backpack. backpack. Put the water bottles in your backpack.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U4-LS3-W02","script":"cliff. cliff. Don't stand near the edge of the cliff.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U4-LS3-W03","script":"wildlife. wildlife. Farasan Islands have amazing wildlife.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U4-LS3-W04","script":"slip. slip. Be careful – you might slip on the wet rocks.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U4-LS3-W05","script":"wander. wander. We wandered around the old village.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U4-LS3-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Hike, Wander, Slip: Outdoor Words and Movement Verbs”. Let’s learn camping and outdoor vocabulary; verbs of movement with shades of meaning (walk, hike, wander, march; climb, crawl, slide, slip) together. Meet some new words. backpack: a bag you carry on your back. cliff: a high, steep rock face. wildlife: animals and plants that live in nature. Outdoor words: camp, tent, campfire, trail, compass, flashlight (American English), sleeping bag, backpack, cliff, wildlife. Movement verbs have shades of meaning. walk (normal) • hike (walk a long way in nature) • wander (walk slowly with no plan) • march (walk in step like soldiers). climb (go up using hands and feet) • crawl (move on hands and knees) • slide (move smoothly on a surface) • slip (slide by accident). Here are some examples. We put up the tent before sunset. The scouts followed the trail to the valley. I crawled into the small cave with my flashlight. Be careful! Some learners say: “We made a tent.” That’s not right. We say: “We put up a tent.” put up a tent. Quick check: Do you slip on purpose or by accident? … Think! … By accident. Great job! Now you can say: I can talk about camping and hiking.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.9"}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U4-LS4","title":"When the Sun Set, We Lit a Fire: Commas with Time Clauses","objectives":["Students will be able to put a comma after a time clause that starts a sentence.","Students will be able to leave out the comma when the time clause comes at the end.","I can write \"When the sun set, we lit a fire.\"","I can write \"We lit a fire when the sun set.\" with no comma."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من وضع فاصلة بعد جملة الزمن في بداية الجملة.","سيتمكن الطلاب من حذف الفاصلة عندما تأتي جملة الزمن في النهاية.","أستطيع أن أكتب When the sun set, we lit a fire.","أستطيع أن أكتب We lit a fire when the sun set. بدون فاصلة."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"camp","pos":"verb / noun","ipa":"/kæmp/","definition":"to stay outside in a tent; a place where people stay in tents","arabic":"يخيّم / مخيم","example":"We camped near the sand dunes.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"tent","pos":"noun","ipa":"/tɛnt/","definition":"a shelter made of cloth that you sleep in outside","arabic":"خيمة","example":"Dad put up the tent before dark.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"campfire","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈkæmpˌfaɪɚ/","definition":"a fire you make outside when you camp","arabic":"نار المخيم","example":"We made tea on the campfire.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"hike","pos":"verb / noun","ipa":"/haɪk/","definition":"to walk a long way in nature; a long walk","arabic":"يتنزّه سيرًا / نزهة طويلة","example":"We hiked to the top of the hill.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"trail","pos":"noun","ipa":"/treɪl/","definition":"a path through the countryside or mountains","arabic":"درب / ممر","example":"Follow the trail to the waterfall.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"compass","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈkʌmpəs/","definition":"a tool that shows north, south, east and west","arabic":"بوصلة","example":"The compass helped us find the way.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"A time clause starts with when, while, before, after or as soon as and has a subject and a verb: when the sun set.\nIf the time clause comes first, put a comma after it: When the sun set, we lit a fire. While we were hiking, we saw a fox.\nIf the time clause comes second, don't use a comma: We lit a fire when the sun set. A time clause alone is not a complete sentence: (not: When the sun set.)\nTime clause first → comma: After we ate, we washed the plates.\nTime clause second → no comma: We washed the plates after we ate.\nA time clause alone is a fragment – join it to a main clause.\nTime words: when • while • before • after • as soon as","examples":["When we reached the top, we took a photo.","We took a photo when we reached the top.","While Dad was cooking, we collected wood.","Before we went to sleep, we checked the tent.","After the storm stopped, the sky was clear.","As soon as the sun rose, we started hiking.","I always pack my backpack before I leave.","While I was crawling into the cave, I hit my head."],"common_errors":["✗ When we arrived we put up the tent. → ✓ When we arrived, we put up the tent. (Comma after the time clause at the start.)","✗ We put up the tent, when we arrived. → ✓ We put up the tent when we arrived. (No comma when the time clause is second.)","✗ While we were hiking. We saw a fox. → ✓ While we were hiking, we saw a fox. (A time clause alone is not a sentence.)","✗ After, we ate we slept. → ✓ After we ate, we slept. (The comma goes after the whole clause.)"],"arabic":"جملة الزمن تبدأ بـ when أو while أو before أو after وفيها فاعل وفعل.\nإذا جاءت جملة الزمن أولًا نضع فاصلة بعدها: When the sun set, we lit a fire.\nإذا جاءت ثانيًا فلا فاصلة: We lit a fire when the sun set.\nجملة الزمن وحدها ليست جملة كاملة."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “When the Sun Set, We Lit a Fire: Commas with Time Clauses”. Let’s learn commas after time clauses at the start of a sentence (When…, While…, Before…, After…) together.","on_screen":"GV-L04-U4-LS4 | When the Sun Set, We Lit a Fire: Commas with Time Clauses","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"A time clause starts with when, while, before, after or as soon as and has a subject and a verb: when the sun set.","on_screen":"commas after time clauses at the start of a sentence (When…, While…, Before…, After…)","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"A time clause starts with when, while, before, after or as soon as and has a subject and a verb: when the sun set. If the time clause comes first, put a comma after it: When the sun set, we lit a fire. While we were hiking, we saw a fox.","on_screen":"Time clause first → comma: After we ate, we washed the plates. • Time clause second → no comma: We washed the plates after we ate. • A time clause alone is a fragment – join it to a main clause.","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. When we reached the top, we took a photo. We took a photo when we reached the top. While Dad was cooking, we collected wood.","on_screen":"When we reached the top, we took a photo. / We took a photo when we reached the top. / While Dad was cooking, we collected wood.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “When we arrived we put up the tent.” That’s not right. We say: “When we arrived, we put up the tent.” Comma after the time clause at the start.","on_screen":"✗ When we arrived we put up the tent.   ✓ When we arrived, we put up the tent.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"After we ate we slept.\" Where is the comma? … Think! … After \"ate\". Great job! Now you can say: I can write \"When the sun set, we lit a fire.\"","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can write \"When the sun set, we lit a fire.\"","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: commas after time clauses at the start of a sentence (When…, While…, Before…, After…).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","جملة الزمن تبدأ بـ when أو while أو before أو after وفيها فاعل وفعل.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: When we arrived we put up the tent. — الصحيح: When we arrived, we put up the tent.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أكتب When the sun set, we lit a fire."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"My Camping Diary (editing passage)","body":"When we arrived at the campsite the wind was blowing hard. While Dad was putting up the tent my brother and I collected wood. We lit a campfire, when it got dark. After we ate dinner we looked at the stars. I fell asleep, while Grandpa was telling a story.","word_count":50,"audio_id":""}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L04-U4-LS4-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct sentence.","items":[{"q":"","options":["When the rain stopped we went, outside.","When the rain, stopped we went outside.","When the rain stopped, we went outside.","When, the rain stopped we went outside."],"answer":"When the rain stopped, we went outside.","explanation":"Time clause first → comma after it.","explanation_ar":"جملة الزمن أولًا ← فاصلة."},{"q":"","options":["We went outside when the rain stopped.","We went outside when, the rain stopped.","We went outside, when the rain stopped.","We went, outside when the rain stopped."],"answer":"We went outside when the rain stopped.","explanation":"Time clause second → no comma.","explanation_ar":"جملة الزمن ثانيًا ← بلا فاصلة."},{"q":"","options":["While we were sleeping a storm, started.","While we were sleeping. A storm started.","While, we were sleeping a storm started.","While we were sleeping, a storm started."],"answer":"While we were sleeping, a storm started.","explanation":"A time clause alone is a fragment – join it.","explanation_ar":"جملة الزمن وحدها ناقصة."},{"q":"","options":["Before, I left I locked the door.","Before I left, I locked the door.","Before I left I, locked the door.","Before I left. I locked the door."],"answer":"Before I left, I locked the door.","explanation":"The comma goes after the whole clause.","explanation_ar":"الفاصلة بعد الجملة كاملة."},{"q":"","options":["I brush my teeth before I go to bed.","I brush my teeth, before I go to bed.","I, brush my teeth before I go to bed.","I brush my teeth before, I go to bed."],"answer":"I brush my teeth before I go to bed.","explanation":"Time clause second → no comma.","explanation_ar":"جملة الزمن ثانيًا ← بلا فاصلة."},{"q":"","options":["As soon as, we arrived it started to rain.","As soon as we arrived. It started to rain.","As soon as we arrived it started, to rain.","As soon as we arrived, it started to rain."],"answer":"As soon as we arrived, it started to rain.","explanation":"Time clause first → comma after it.","explanation_ar":"جملة الزمن أولًا ← فاصلة."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U4-LS4-B1","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Add or remove a comma.","items":[{"q":"When I saw the snake I ran back to the tent.","options":[],"answer":"When I saw the snake, I ran back to the tent.","explanation":"(add) → ,. Time clause first → comma after it.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → ,. جملة الزمن أولًا ← فاصلة."},{"q":"We lit the campfire, after the sun went down.","options":[],"answer":"We lit the campfire after the sun went down.","explanation":", → (delete). Time clause second → no comma.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: , → (delete). جملة الزمن ثانيًا ← بلا فاصلة."},{"q":"While we were eating a fox came near the tent.","options":[],"answer":"While we were eating, a fox came near the tent.","explanation":"(add) → ,. Time clause first → comma after it.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → ,. جملة الزمن أولًا ← فاصلة."},{"q":"After we finished the hike we were very tired.","options":[],"answer":"After we finished the hike, we were very tired.","explanation":"(add) → ,. Time clause first → comma after it.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → ,. جملة الزمن أولًا ← فاصلة."},{"q":"I turned on my flashlight, when it got dark.","options":[],"answer":"I turned on my flashlight when it got dark.","explanation":", → (delete). Time clause second → no comma.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: , → (delete). جملة الزمن ثانيًا ← بلا فاصلة."},{"q":"Before we left the camp we cleaned everything.","options":[],"answer":"Before we left the camp, we cleaned everything.","explanation":"(add) → ,. Time clause first → comma after it.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → ,. جملة الزمن أولًا ← فاصلة."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U4-LS4-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Edit the adventure diary.","items":[{"q":"When we arrived at the campsite the wind was blowing hard.","options":[],"answer":"When we arrived at the campsite, the wind was blowing hard.","explanation":"(add) → ,. Time clause first → comma after it.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → ,. جملة الزمن أولًا ← فاصلة."},{"q":"When we arrived at the campsite the wind was blowing hard.","options":[],"answer":"When we arrived at the campsite, the wind was blowing hard.","explanation":"(add) → ,. Time clause first → comma after it.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → ,. جملة الزمن أولًا ← فاصلة."},{"q":"We lit a campfire, when it got dark.","options":[],"answer":"We lit a campfire when it got dark.","explanation":", → (delete). Time clause first → comma after it.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: , → (delete). جملة الزمن أولًا ← فاصلة."},{"q":"When we arrived at the campsite the wind was blowing hard.","options":[],"answer":"When we arrived at the campsite, the wind was blowing hard.","explanation":"(add) → ,. Time clause first → comma after it.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → ,. جملة الزمن أولًا ← فاصلة."},{"q":"We lit a campfire, when it got dark.","options":[],"answer":"We lit a campfire when it got dark.","explanation":", → (delete). Time clause first → comma after it.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: , → (delete). جملة الزمن أولًا ← فاصلة."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U4-LS4-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write with time clauses.","items":[{"q":"Write 2 sentences that start with When or While (with a comma).","options":[],"answer":"When I got home, I ate lunch. While I was reading, my cat sat on my book.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses commas after time clauses at the start of a sentence (When…, While…, Before…, After…) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write the same 2 ideas with the time clause at the end (no comma).","options":[],"answer":"I ate lunch when I got home. My cat sat on my book while I was reading.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses commas after time clauses at the start of a sentence (When…, While…, Before…, After…) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Fix this fragment: \"After we hiked to the top.\"","options":[],"answer":"After we hiked to the top, we rested.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses commas after time clauses at the start of a sentence (When…, While…, Before…, After…) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Word Builder","mechanic":"word_builder","rules":["The teacher reads a word and a short clue.","Teams build the word with letter tiles in 30 seconds.","The team holds up the word; correct spelling = 1 point, with correct capital letter or punctuation where needed = 1 bonus point.","Continue until all words are used."],"data":[{"word":"tent","clue":"a shelter made of cloth that you sleep in outside"},{"word":"campfire","clue":"a fire you make outside when you camp"},{"word":"compass","clue":"a tool that shows north, south, east and west"},{"word":"flashlight","clue":"a small light you hold in your hand (American English)"},{"word":"backpack","clue":"a bag you carry on your back"},{"word":"wildlife","clue":"animals and plants that live in nature"},{"word":"camp","clue":"to stay outside in a tent; a place where people stay in tents"},{"word":"hike","clue":"to walk a long way in nature; a long walk"},{"word":"trail","clue":"a path through the countryside or mountains"},{"word":"cliff","clue":"a high, steep rock face"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"","options":["When Dad called I was, reading.","When Dad called, I was reading.","When Dad called. I was reading.","When, Dad called I was reading."],"answer":"When Dad called, I was reading.","explanation":"Time clause first → comma after it.","explanation_ar":"جملة الزمن أولًا ← فاصلة."},{"q":"","options":["I was reading, when Dad called.","I was reading when Dad called.","I was reading when, Dad called.","I was, reading when Dad called."],"answer":"I was reading when Dad called.","explanation":"Time clause second → no comma.","explanation_ar":"جملة الزمن ثانيًا ← بلا فاصلة."},{"q":"Where does the comma go? \"After we ate lunch we went hiking.\"","options":["after \"we\"","after \"After\"","after \"lunch\"","after \"went\""],"answer":"after \"lunch\"","explanation":"The comma goes after the whole clause.","explanation_ar":"الفاصلة بعد الجملة كاملة."},{"q":"Which one is a fragment (not a complete sentence)?","options":["While we were walking, we saw a deer.","While we were walking in the forest.","We were walking in the forest.","We saw a deer while we were walking."],"answer":"While we were walking in the forest.","explanation":"A time clause alone is a fragment – join it.","explanation_ar":"جملة الزمن وحدها ناقصة."},{"q":"","options":["Before we went camping. We bought a new tent.","Before we went camping we bought, a new tent.","Before, we went camping we bought a new tent.","Before we went camping, we bought a new tent."],"answer":"Before we went camping, we bought a new tent.","explanation":"Time clause first → comma after it.","explanation_ar":"جملة الزمن أولًا ← فاصلة."},{"q":"","options":["We sang songs while we were driving.","We sang songs, while we were driving.","We sang, songs while we were driving.","We sang songs while, we were driving."],"answer":"We sang songs while we were driving.","explanation":"Time clause second → no comma.","explanation_ar":"جملة الزمن ثانيًا ← بلا فاصلة."},{"q":"","options":["As soon, as the bell rang the students went out.","As soon as the bell rang the students, went out.","As soon as the bell rang. The students went out.","As soon as the bell rang, the students went out."],"answer":"As soon as the bell rang, the students went out.","explanation":"Time clause first → comma after it.","explanation_ar":"جملة الزمن أولًا ← فاصلة."},{"q":"Find the sentence with a missing comma.","options":["We went inside at night.","It got dark quickly.","When it got dark we went inside.","We went inside when it got dark."],"answer":"When it got dark we went inside.","explanation":"Time clause first → comma after it.","explanation_ar":"جملة الزمن أولًا ← فاصلة."},{"q":"","options":["While I was climbing, my foot slipped.","While, I was climbing my foot slipped.","While I was climbing. My foot slipped.","While I was climbing my foot, slipped."],"answer":"While I was climbing, my foot slipped.","explanation":"A time clause alone is a fragment – join it.","explanation_ar":"جملة الزمن وحدها ناقصة."},{"q":"","options":["The birds flew away when, we came closer.","The birds flew, away when we came closer.","The birds flew away when we came closer.","The birds flew away, when we came closer."],"answer":"The birds flew away when we came closer.","explanation":"Time clause second → no comma.","explanation_ar":"جملة الزمن ثانيًا ← بلا فاصلة."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L04-U4-LS4-IMG01","prompt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “Adventures Outdoors” that shows commas after time clauses at the start of a sentence (When…, While…, Before…, After…) in action. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “Adventures Outdoors” that shows commas after time clauses at the start of a sentence (When…, While…, Before…, After…) in action"},{"id":"GV-L04-U4-LS4-IMG02","prompt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen"},{"id":"GV-L04-U4-LS4-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Word Builder”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Word Builder"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U4-LS4-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “When the Sun Set, We Lit a Fire: Commas with Time Clauses”. Let’s learn commas after time clauses at the start of a sentence (When…, While…, Before…, After…) together. A time clause starts with when, while, before, after or as soon as and has a subject and a verb: when the sun set. A time clause starts with when, while, before, after or as soon as and has a subject and a verb: when the sun set. If the time clause comes first, put a comma after it: When the sun set, we lit a fire. While we were hiking, we saw a fox. Here are some examples. When we reached the top, we took a photo. We took a photo when we reached the top. While Dad was cooking, we collected wood. Be careful! Some learners say: “When we arrived we put up the tent.” That’s not right. We say: “When we arrived, we put up the tent.” Comma after the time clause at the start. Quick check: \"After we ate we slept.\" Where is the comma? … Think! … After \"ate\". Great job! Now you can say: I can write \"When the sun set, we lit a fire.\"","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.9"}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U4-LS5","title":"An Adventure Story: Language in Use","objectives":["Students will be able to tell an adventure story with background and interrupting actions.","Students will be able to write an adventure story with past tenses, precise verbs and commas with time clauses.","I can tell an adventure story.","I can write an adventure story with when and while."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من حكاية قصة مغامرة مع الأحداث الخلفية والأحداث المقاطعة.","سيتمكن الطلاب من كتابة قصة مغامرة بأزمنة الماضي والأفعال الدقيقة والفواصل مع جمل الزمن.","أستطيع أن أحكي قصة مغامرة.","أستطيع أن أكتب قصة مغامرة باستخدام when وwhile."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"camp","pos":"verb / noun","ipa":"/kæmp/","definition":"to stay outside in a tent; a place where people stay in tents","arabic":"يخيّم / مخيم","example":"We camped near the sand dunes.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"tent","pos":"noun","ipa":"/tɛnt/","definition":"a shelter made of cloth that you sleep in outside","arabic":"خيمة","example":"Dad put up the tent before dark.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"campfire","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈkæmpˌfaɪɚ/","definition":"a fire you make outside when you camp","arabic":"نار المخيم","example":"We made tea on the campfire.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"hike","pos":"verb / noun","ipa":"/haɪk/","definition":"to walk a long way in nature; a long walk","arabic":"يتنزّه سيرًا / نزهة طويلة","example":"We hiked to the top of the hill.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"trail","pos":"noun","ipa":"/treɪl/","definition":"a path through the countryside or mountains","arabic":"درب / ممر","example":"Follow the trail to the waterfall.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"compass","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈkʌmpəs/","definition":"a tool that shows north, south, east and west","arabic":"بوصلة","example":"The compass helped us find the way.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"flashlight","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈflæʃˌlaɪt/","definition":"a small light you hold in your hand (American English)","arabic":"مصباح يدوي","example":"Turn on your flashlight in the cave.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"sleeping bag","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈslipɪŋ bæɡ/","definition":"a warm bag you sleep in when you camp","arabic":"كيس نوم","example":"My sleeping bag kept me warm all night.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"backpack","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈbækˌpæk/","definition":"a bag you carry on your back","arabic":"حقيبة ظهر","example":"Put the water bottles in your backpack.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"cliff","pos":"noun","ipa":"/klɪf/","definition":"a high, steep rock face","arabic":"جرف / منحدر صخري","example":"Don't stand near the edge of the cliff.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"wildlife","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈwaɪldˌlaɪf/","definition":"animals and plants that live in nature","arabic":"الحياة البرية","example":"Farasan Islands have amazing wildlife.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"slip","pos":"verb","ipa":"/slɪp/","definition":"to slide by accident and almost fall","arabic":"ينزلق","example":"Be careful – you might slip on the wet rocks.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"wander","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˈwɑndɚ/","definition":"to walk slowly with no special plan","arabic":"يتجوّل","example":"We wandered around the old village.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"Today you use all of Unit 4: the past continuous, the past simple, when/while, outdoor words, precise movement verbs and commas with time clauses.\nA good adventure story starts by setting the scene (past continuous), then something happens (past simple), and it ends with a lesson or feeling.\n✔ setting the scene: The sun was shining…\n✔ interruption: …when Adam slipped.\n✔ while + past continuous; when + past simple\n✔ When/While clause first → comma","examples":["The wind was blowing across the dunes.","We were crawling through a narrow cave when we saw a bat.","While we were watching the sunset, a camel walked past our tent.","When the storm started, we ran into the tent.","My brother slipped on the wet rocks.","We hiked along the trail for two hours.","I was holding the flashlight when it stopped working.","After we found the path, we felt safe again."],"common_errors":["✗ We hiked when we were seeing a snake. → ✓ We were hiking when we saw a snake. (Long action → past continuous; short → past simple.)","✗ When we got lost we used the compass. → ✓ When we got lost, we used the compass. (Comma after the time clause at the start.)","✗ The sun was shine. → ✓ The sun was shining. (was + verb-ing.)"],"arabic":"نراجع الماضي المستمر والماضي البسيط وwhen/while وكلمات الطبيعة والفواصل.\nقصة المغامرة: نرسم المشهد بالماضي المستمر، ثم يحدث شيء مفاجئ بالماضي البسيط، ثم الخاتمة.\nتذكّر الفاصلة بعد جملة الزمن في بداية الجملة."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “An Adventure Story: Language in Use”. Let’s learn past continuous and past simple, when/while, outdoor words and commas with time clauses (unit review) together.","on_screen":"GV-L04-U4-LS5 | An Adventure Story: Language in Use","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Story dice: roll a die for a setting (desert, mountain, beach, forest, cave, island). In pairs, tell a story: set the scene with 2 past continuous sentences, then add a surprise with \"when\" or \"while\".","on_screen":"Language in use","visual":"Split screen: two cast members talking, with speech bubbles appearing."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Today you use all of Unit 4: the past continuous, the past simple, when/while, outdoor words, precise movement verbs and commas with time clauses. A good adventure story starts by setting the scene (past continuous), then something happens (past simple), and it ends with a lesson or feeling.","on_screen":"✔ setting the scene: The sun was shining… • ✔ interruption: …when Adam slipped. • ✔ while + past continuous; when + past simple","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. The wind was blowing across the dunes. We were crawling through a narrow cave when we saw a bat. While we were watching the sunset, a camel walked past our tent.","on_screen":"The wind was blowing across the dunes. / We were crawling through a narrow cave when we saw a bat. / While we were watching the sunset, a camel walked past our tent.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “We hiked when we were seeing a snake.” That’s not right. We say: “We were hiking when we saw a snake.” Long action → past continuous; short → past simple.","on_screen":"✗ We hiked when we were seeing a snake.   ✓ We were hiking when we saw a snake.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: what is wrong with “When we got lost we used the compass.”? … Think! … It should be “When we got lost, we used the compass.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can tell an adventure story.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can tell an adventure story.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: past continuous and past simple, when/while, outdoor words and commas with time clauses (unit review).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نراجع الماضي المستمر والماضي البسيط وwhen/while وكلمات الطبيعة والفواصل.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: We hiked when we were seeing a snake. — الصحيح: We were hiking when we saw a snake.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أحكي قصة مغامرة."]},"texts":[{"type":"model","title":"Lost in the Mountains – Yusuf","body":"Last summer, Adam and I were hiking near Abha. The sun was shining, and birds were singing in the trees.\nWhile we were following the trail, thick clouds came down the mountain. We couldn't see the path!\nWe were walking slowly when Adam slipped on a wet rock. Luckily, he wasn't hurt.\nWhen the clouds moved away, I checked my compass. We were going the wrong way!\nWe turned around and hiked back to the car.\nNow I always check the weather before I go hiking.","word_count":86,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U4-LS5-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L04-U4-LS5-A1","type":"true_false","instructions":"Controlled practice: Read Yusuf's story. True or False?","items":[{"q":"Yusuf and Adam were hiking near Abha.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “Lost in the Mountains – Yusuf”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"It was raining when they started the hike.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “Lost in the Mountains – Yusuf”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Clouds came down while they were following the trail.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “Lost in the Mountains – Yusuf”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Adam slipped on a wet rock and broke his leg.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “Lost in the Mountains – Yusuf”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Yusuf used a compass.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “Lost in the Mountains – Yusuf”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"They were going the right way.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “Lost in the Mountains – Yusuf”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U4-LS5-B1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Guided practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"At the start, the birds ___ in the trees.","options":["was singing","were singing","sang singing","were sing"],"answer":"were singing","explanation":"Background action → past continuous.","explanation_ar":"الخلفية ← الماضي المستمر."},{"q":"They were walking slowly when Adam ___.","options":["was slipping","slips","slip","slipped"],"answer":"slipped","explanation":"Short action / event → past simple.","explanation_ar":"الحدث القصير ← الماضي البسيط."},{"q":"___ they were following the trail, clouds came down.","options":["While","When","During","Than"],"answer":"While","explanation":"while + long action; when + short action.","explanation_ar":"while وwhen."},{"q":"Yusuf checked his ___ to find the way.","options":["campfire","sleeping bag","compass","tent"],"answer":"compass","explanation":"Precise outdoor or movement word.","explanation_ar":"الكلمة الدقيقة."},{"q":"","options":["When the clouds moved away. I checked my compass.","When, the clouds moved away I checked my compass.","When the clouds moved away I checked, my compass.","When the clouds moved away, I checked my compass."],"answer":"When the clouds moved away, I checked my compass.","explanation":"Time clause first → comma.","explanation_ar":"الفاصلة بعد جملة الزمن."},{"q":"They ___ back to the car.","options":["marched","hiked","slid","crawled"],"answer":"hiked","explanation":"Precise outdoor or movement word.","explanation_ar":"الكلمة الدقيقة."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U4-LS5-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Story dice. Write your story notes.","items":[{"q":"Setting (from the die): ___","options":[],"answer":"a cave near the coast","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past continuous and past simple, when/while, outdoor words and commas with time clauses (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Set the scene (past continuous, 2 sentences): ___","options":[],"answer":"The waves were crashing. We were looking for shells.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past continuous and past simple, when/while, outdoor words and commas with time clauses (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"The surprise (when/while): ___","options":[],"answer":"While we were exploring the cave, the water started to rise.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past continuous and past simple, when/while, outdoor words and commas with time clauses (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"What did you do? (past simple): ___","options":[],"answer":"We climbed onto a high rock.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past continuous and past simple, when/while, outdoor words and commas with time clauses (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"The ending: ___","options":[],"answer":"When the water went down, we walked out safely.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past continuous and past simple, when/while, outdoor words and commas with time clauses (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U4-LS5-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write your adventure story.","items":[{"q":"Plan: setting, scene, surprise, actions, ending.","options":[],"answer":"desert at night; stars shining, fire burning; a strange light appeared; we followed it; it was a car with our uncle","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past continuous and past simple, when/while, outdoor words and commas with time clauses (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write your story in 7–8 sentences.","options":[],"answer":"Last winter, we were camping in the desert. The stars were shining, and the fire was burning. While we were drinking tea, a strange light appeared. We walked slowly towards it. When we got closer, we heard a horn. It was my uncle's car! He was bringing us dinner. It was the best surprise of the trip.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past continuous and past simple, when/while, outdoor words and commas with time clauses (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Check: past continuous for the scene? when/while? commas? Fix one mistake.","options":[],"answer":"I changed \"When we got closer we heard\" to \"When we got closer, we heard\".","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past continuous and past simple, when/while, outdoor words and commas with time clauses (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Quiz Show Challenge","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["Teams take turns choosing a category and a cue word.","Grammar: make a sentence with past continuous and past simple, when/while, outdoor words and commas with time clauses (unit review). Words: give the meaning. Spelling: spell it. Write It!: write a sentence with correct punctuation.","Correct answers score 10 points; teams may steal a question another team misses.","The highest score after 8 minutes wins."],"data":[{"cue":"camp","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"tent","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"campfire","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"hike","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"trail","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"compass","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"flashlight","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"sleeping bag","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"backpack","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"cliff","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"wildlife","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"slip","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"wander","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"It was a cold night. The wind ___.","options":["blew blowing","were blowing","was blow","was blowing"],"answer":"was blowing","explanation":"Background action → past continuous.","explanation_ar":"الخلفية ← الماضي المستمر."},{"q":"I was taking a photo when the camel ___.","options":["ran away","run away","runs away","was running away"],"answer":"ran away","explanation":"Short action / event → past simple.","explanation_ar":"الحدث القصير ← الماضي البسيط."},{"q":"___ the bus was moving, we sang songs.","options":["Since","During","While","When"],"answer":"While","explanation":"while + long action; when + short action.","explanation_ar":"while وwhen."},{"q":"The children ___ down the sand dune on boards.","options":["crawled","slid","slipped","marched"],"answer":"slid","explanation":"Precise outdoor or movement word.","explanation_ar":"الكلمة الدقيقة."},{"q":"","options":["While we were camping, it rained all night.","While we camped, it was rain all night.","While we were camping it rained, all night.","While we were camping. It rained all night."],"answer":"While we were camping, it rained all night.","explanation":"Time clause first → comma.","explanation_ar":"الفاصلة بعد جملة الزمن."},{"q":"","options":["We sleeping when the storm started.","We were sleep when the storm started.","We slept when the storm was starting.","We were sleeping when the storm started."],"answer":"We were sleeping when the storm started.","explanation":"Short action / event → past simple.","explanation_ar":"الحدث القصير ← الماضي البسيط."},{"q":"Bring a ___ – it gets dark early.","options":["cliff","trail","compass","flashlight"],"answer":"flashlight","explanation":"Precise outdoor or movement word.","explanation_ar":"الكلمة الدقيقة."},{"q":"","options":["When we were reaching the beach, the sun set.","When we reached the beach, the sun was setting.","When we reached the beach the sun was setting,","When we reached the beach. The sun was setting."],"answer":"When we reached the beach, the sun was setting.","explanation":"Time clause first → comma.","explanation_ar":"الفاصلة بعد جملة الزمن."},{"q":"What were you doing when I called? – I ___ my bike.","options":["were fixing","fix","was fixing","fixed fixing"],"answer":"was fixing","explanation":"Background action → past continuous.","explanation_ar":"الخلفية ← الماضي المستمر."},{"q":"Pick the best opening for an adventure story:","options":["The wind was howl, and the waves were crash on the rocks.","The wind was howling, and the waves were crashing on the rocks.","The wind were howling, and the waves was crashing on the rocks.","The wind howling, and the waves crashing on the rocks."],"answer":"The wind was howling, and the waves were crashing on the rocks.","explanation":"Background action → past continuous.","explanation_ar":"الخلفية ← الماضي المستمر."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L04-U4-LS5-IMG01","prompt":"Yusuf and Adam on a rocky trail in the Asir mountains, one boy pointing at baboons on a cliff while the other holds a compass, clouds rolling in. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Yusuf and Adam on a rocky trail in the Asir mountains, one boy pointing at baboons on a cliff while the other holds a compass, clouds rolling in"},{"id":"GV-L04-U4-LS5-IMG02","prompt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “Adventures Outdoors”, speech bubbles left empty. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “Adventures Outdoors”, speech bubbles left empty"},{"id":"GV-L04-U4-LS5-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Quiz Show Challenge”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Quiz Show Challenge"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U4-LS5-T1","script":"Last summer, Adam and I were hiking near Abha. The sun was shining, and birds were singing in the trees. While we were following the trail, thick clouds came down the mountain. We couldn't see the path! We were walking slowly when Adam slipped on a wet rock. Luckily, he wasn't hurt. When the clouds moved away, I checked my compass. We were going the wrong way! We turned around and hiked back to the car. Now I always check the weather before I go hiking.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U4-LS5-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “An Adventure Story: Language in Use”. Let’s learn past continuous and past simple, when/while, outdoor words and commas with time clauses (unit review) together. Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Story dice: roll a die for a setting (desert, mountain, beach, forest, cave, island). In pairs, tell a story: set the scene with 2 past continuous sentences, then add a surprise with \"when\" or \"while\". Today you use all of Unit 4: the past continuous, the past simple, when/while, outdoor words, precise movement verbs and commas with time clauses. A good adventure story starts by setting the scene (past continuous), then something happens (past simple), and it ends with a lesson or feeling. Here are some examples. The wind was blowing across the dunes. We were crawling through a narrow cave when we saw a bat. While we were watching the sunset, a camel walked past our tent. Be careful! Some learners say: “We hiked when we were seeing a snake.” That’s not right. We say: “We were hiking when we saw a snake.” Long action → past continuous; short → past simple. Quick check: what is wrong with “When we got lost we used the compass.”? … Think! … It should be “When we got lost, we used the compass.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can tell an adventure story.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.9"}]}],"unit_test":[{"q":"At 8 p.m., my mom ___ dinner.","options":["was cooking","was cook","were cooking","cooked cooking"],"answer":"was cooking","explanation":"I / he / she / it → was + verb-ing.","explanation_ar":"was مع المفرد."},{"q":"The boys ___ in the sea at noon.","options":["were swim","swimming was","were swimming","was swimming"],"answer":"were swimming","explanation":"you / we / they → were + verb-ing.","explanation_ar":"were مع الجمع."},{"q":"","options":["It was snow when we woke up.","It were snowing when we woke up.","It snowing when we woke up.","It was snowing when we woke up."],"answer":"It was snowing when we woke up.","explanation":"Add -ing to the main verb.","explanation_ar":"أضف ing."},{"q":"We ___ paying attention. Sorry!","options":["wasn't","aren't","didn't","weren't"],"answer":"weren't","explanation":"wasn't / weren't + verb-ing.","explanation_ar":"النفي."},{"q":"","options":["What were you do at seven?","What you were doing at seven?","What were you doing at seven?","What did you doing at seven?"],"answer":"What were you doing at seven?","explanation":"Was/Were + subject + verb-ing?","explanation_ar":"السؤال."},{"q":"I ___ my homework when the lights went off.","options":["was doing","were doing","did","do"],"answer":"was doing","explanation":"Long background action → past continuous.","explanation_ar":"الفعل الطويل ← الماضي المستمر."},{"q":"We were driving to Taif when we ___ baboons.","options":["were seeing","was seeing","saw","see"],"answer":"saw","explanation":"Short action that interrupts → past simple.","explanation_ar":"الفعل القصير ← الماضي البسيط."},{"q":"___ I was waiting for the bus, I read a book.","options":["When","Then","While","During"],"answer":"While","explanation":"while + past continuous.","explanation_ar":"while + الماضي المستمر."},{"q":"","options":["While Dad was reading, Mom knitting.","While Dad was reading, Mom was knitting.","While Dad was read, Mom was knitting.","While Dad read, Mom was knit."],"answer":"While Dad was reading, Mom was knitting.","explanation":"Two long actions at the same time → past continuous + past continuous.","explanation_ar":"فعلان طويلان معًا."},{"q":"","options":["He was hurting his knee when he played football.","He hurted his knee when he was playing football.","He hurt his knee when he was playing football.","He hurt his knee when he playing football."],"answer":"He hurt his knee when he was playing football.","explanation":"Short action that interrupts → past simple.","explanation_ar":"الفعل القصير ← الماضي البسيط."},{"q":"We ___ the tent near the trees.","options":["built on","did","made","put up"],"answer":"put up","explanation":"Use the right outdoor collocation.","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة الصحيحة."},{"q":"The baby ___ across the carpet on her hands and knees.","options":["slipped","crawled","marched","hiked"],"answer":"crawled","explanation":"Choose the movement verb with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"فعل الحركة المناسب."},{"q":"Be careful! You might ___ on the ice.","options":["march","slip","hike","wander"],"answer":"slip","explanation":"Choose the movement verb with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"فعل الحركة المناسب."},{"q":"A tool that shows directions is a ___.","options":["flashlight","backpack","compass","tent"],"answer":"compass","explanation":"Choose the camping word that fits.","explanation_ar":"كلمة التخييم المناسبة."},{"q":"We ___ for five kilometers up the mountain.","options":["hiked","crawled","wandered off","slid"],"answer":"hiked","explanation":"Choose the movement verb with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"فعل الحركة المناسب."},{"q":"Animals and plants in nature are called ___.","options":["campfires","wildlife","trails","cliffs"],"answer":"wildlife","explanation":"Choose the camping word that fits.","explanation_ar":"كلمة التخييم المناسبة."},{"q":"","options":["When we heard the thunder, we ran inside.","When we heard the thunder we ran, inside.","When we heard the thunder. We ran inside.","When, we heard the thunder we ran inside."],"answer":"When we heard the thunder, we ran inside.","explanation":"Time clause first → comma after it.","explanation_ar":"جملة الزمن أولًا ← فاصلة."},{"q":"","options":["We ran inside, when we heard the thunder.","We ran inside when, we heard the thunder.","We ran, inside when we heard the thunder.","We ran inside when we heard the thunder."],"answer":"We ran inside when we heard the thunder.","explanation":"Time clause second → no comma.","explanation_ar":"جملة الزمن ثانيًا ← بلا فاصلة."},{"q":"Which one is a fragment?","options":["We finished the hike.","We rested after we finished the hike.","After we finished the hike, we rested.","After we finished the hike."],"answer":"After we finished the hike.","explanation":"A time clause alone is a fragment – join it.","explanation_ar":"جملة الزمن وحدها ناقصة."},{"q":"Where does the comma go? \"Before the sun rose we packed our bags.\"","options":["after \"we\"","after \"rose\"","after \"packed\"","after \"Before\""],"answer":"after \"rose\"","explanation":"The comma goes after the whole clause.","explanation_ar":"الفاصلة بعد الجملة كاملة."},{"q":"","options":["As soon as I got home, I took a shower.","As soon, as I got home I took a shower.","As soon as I got home. I took a shower.","As soon as I got home I took, a shower."],"answer":"As soon as I got home, I took a shower.","explanation":"Time clause first → comma after it.","explanation_ar":"جملة الزمن أولًا ← فاصلة."},{"q":"Pick the best sentence for an adventure story:","options":["While we were exploring the cave, we heard a loud noise.","While we were exploring the cave we heard, a loud noise.","While we explored the cave, we were hearing a loud noise.","While we were explore the cave, we heard a loud noise."],"answer":"While we were exploring the cave, we heard a loud noise.","explanation":"while + past continuous.","explanation_ar":"while + الماضي المستمر."},{"q":"How can we fix it? \"when we was hiking we see a fox.\"","options":["When we were hiking we see a fox.","When we was hiking, we saw a fox.","when we were hiking, we saw a fox.","When we were hiking, we saw a fox."],"answer":"When we were hiking, we saw a fox.","explanation":"you / we / they → were + verb-ing.","explanation_ar":"were مع الجمع."},{"q":"What was happening when you arrived? – ___","options":["Everyone were eating lunch.","Everyone was eating lunch.","Everyone ate lunch was.","Everyone was eat lunch."],"answer":"Everyone was eating lunch.","explanation":"I / he / she / it → was + verb-ing.","explanation_ar":"was مع المفرد."}],"theme_ar":"مغامرات في الطبيعة","essential_question_ar":"ماذا يمكن أن نتعلم من المغامرات في الطبيعة؟","can_do":"I can describe what was happening in the past and tell an adventure story with the past continuous and past simple.","can_do_ar":"أستطيع أن أصف ما كان يحدث في الماضي وأحكي قصة مغامرة باستخدام الماضي المستمر والماضي البسيط."});
